<div class="stats-section">
  <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
    <button 
      class="tab active" 
      role="tab" 
      aria-selected="true" 
      aria-controls="ewr-panel"
      id="ewr-tab"
      data-location="ewr"
    >
      <span class="tab-title">EWR</span>
      <span class="tab-subtitle">US East Newark</span>
    </button>
    <button 
      class="tab" 
      role="tab" 
      aria-selected="false" 
      aria-controls="lax-panel"
      id="lax-tab"
      data-location="lax"
    >
      <span class="tab-title">LAX</span>
      <span class="tab-subtitle">US West Los Angeles</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div id="ewr-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ewr-tab" class="tab-panel active">
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">✓</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="ewr-health">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Health</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">👥</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="ewr-ips">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">IPs (7 days)</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="ewr-p50">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Latency p50</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="ewr-p95">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Latency p95</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="history-section" id="ewr-history" style="display: none;">
      <h3>Recent History</h3>
      <div class="history-table-wrapper">
        <table class="history-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Date</th>
              <th>IPs</th>
              <th>p50 Latency</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="ewr-history-body">
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="lax-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="lax-tab" class="tab-panel">
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">✓</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="lax-health">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Health</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">👥</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="lax-ips">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">IPs (7 days)</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="lax-p50">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Latency p50</div>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="stat-value" data-stat="lax-p95">—</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Latency p95</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="history-section" id="lax-history" style="display: none;">
      <h3>Recent History</h3>
      <div class="history-table-wrapper">
        <table class="history-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Date</th>
              <th>IPs</th>
              <th>p50 Latency</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="lax-history-body">
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section">
    <h2>About These Numbers</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Health:</strong> Service status is automatically monitored. A resolver is considered healthy when it 
      responds to DNS queries within acceptable latency thresholds.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>IPs (7 days):</strong> Count of distinct source IP addresses that have queried this resolver in the 
      past 7 days. This is the only data point we retain, and it is automatically deleted after 7 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Latency p50 / p95:</strong> 50th and 95th percentile query response times in milliseconds. These 
      represent typical and worst-case performance.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Privacy:</strong> No query names are logged. We do not record which domains you request. Source IPs 
      are counted for rate limits and capacity planning only, then deleted after 7 days.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
